dressbook><name>HAYASHI, ZITUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUROKI, YUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNE, JO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHNO, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOSE, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A pressure regulating mechanism for hole sealing plate capable of preventing a pressure vessel from being exploded by an abnormally increased pressure inside the pressure vessel for cells and capacitors even if the pressure vessel is not provided with a rubber burst plate with which it is difficult to control a burst pressure, comprising a burst plate (7) formed integrally with a resin hole sealing plate body (2) which closes the opening of the pressure vessel, a thin wall part (8) smaller in thickness than that of the burst plate (7) and formed integrally between the hole sealing plate body (2) and the burst plate (7), and an inclined surface part (9) which gradually increases in its thickness from the thickness of the thin wall part (8) and is positioned on the peripheral edge part of the burst plate (7).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un mécanisme de régulation de pression d'une plaque d'étanchéité pouvant empêcher un appareil sous pression d'exploser en raison d'une pression anormalement élevée à l'intérieur de l'appareil sous pression pour cellules et condensateurs, même si l'appareil sous pression ne possède pas de plaque d'éclatement en caoutchouc, ce qui rend difficile la gestion d'un éclatement sous pression. Le mécanisme comprend une plaque d'éclatement (7) entièrement formée d'un corps de plaque d'étanchéité en résine (2) bouchant l'ouverture de l'appareil sous pression, une paroi mince (8) moins épaisse que celle de la plaque d'éclatement (7) et située entre le corps de plaque d'étanchéité (2) et la plaque d'éclatement (7), et une surface inclinée (9) qui s'épaissit progressivement selon l'épaisseur de la paroi mince (8) et qui se situe sur le rebord périphérique de la plaque d'éclatement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>